  "sharedModel": [
    "Reuse fixed-unit splitting and CSS-pixel factors for bare numbers, px/in/cm/mm/pt/pc/q. Geometry still validates resolved finite int32 coordinates; it does not use the root/translation float clamp.",
    "Viewport dimensions retain double percentage multiplication/division. Oval/rectangle coordinates retain the existing float percentage stage and their axis/diagonal bases. Line percentages and font-relative geometry remain unsupported.",
    "Root positions remain inert finite lengths with no geometry int32 cap. Fixed sign/extent checks remain consumer-owned.",
    "Local use validates the shared length first, strips every admitted suffix before the native float-number reread, applies the factor and retains the fallback for overflowing intermediate mantissa place values.",
    "Pattern parsing, paint eligibility and supplied-font discovery consume the same fixed-coordinate reader. Rename the former rectangle-only reader and diagnostic to describe its actual shared role.",
    "A centred rotation contributes translate-to-centre, rotate and translate-back. A preceding axis list stores the first translation as floats before rotation promotes it. Already-promoted lists retain double composition. Preserve the former final-domain gate as well as the staged result gate; no pattern-specific sampling adjustment."
  ],
